  "title": "Exact Condition-Number Asymptotics for Four Matrices in Sylvester Example 6",
  "batch_label": "56",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For the four matrices X_i(delta) frozen in source.md and problem.md, for every 0<delta<=1 all four are nonsingular and their spectral condition numbers have exact asymptotic pairs (p_i,K_i) defined by kappa_2(X_i(delta)) ~ K_i delta^{-p_i}: (p_1,K_1)=(2,27); (p_2,K_2)=(1,sqrt(778752/(57905-5*sqrt(132562057)))); (p_3,K_3)=(0,sqrt(rho_3/rho_1)), where rho_1<rho_2<rho_3 are the three roots of 45542974464 z^3-13786630308 z^2+429202697 z-330625, uniquely isolated respectively in (1/1300,1/1200), (1/30,1/29), and (1/4,1/3); and (p_4,K_4)=(0,13/3). Moreover, case 1 obeys |kappa_2/(27 delta^-2)-1|<=121 delta/243 on (0,1]; case 2 obeys the explicit algebraic linear relative-error bound with M_2 and delta_2 defined in evidence/exact_asymptotics.md; case 3 obeys the explicit algebraic linear relative-error bound with M_3 there for 0<delta<=1/10; and case 4 satisfies kappa_2=13/(3+delta) and relative error at most delta/3 on (0,1].",
